## Testing approach

Prefer tests at the outermost meaningful boundary. Protect externally observable contracts without coupling tests to private implementation details. Use lower-level tests only when they are needed to cover unusually risky internals.

## Responsibility

Independently review the complete execution plan. Do not modify files or rewrite the plan yourself.

Inspect the relevant project documentation and repository code. Verify the plan against the confirmed feature and approved design rather than trusting its summary.

